  "published": "2026-04-25T01:13:25.527Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.5 stable: Two fixes + dep-bump to SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.6. (1) `TrackerSignalingServer._readOpts` sets `TypeInfoResolver = new DefaultJsonTypeInfoResolver()` (AOT/trimmed/file-based host compat). (2) `TrackerSignalingServer.HandleWebSocketAsync` skips the Origin allowlist check when the Origin header is empty - non-browser clients (desktop C#, Node.js `ws`, curl) don't send Origin; the allowlist is documented as browser-only abuse protection; empty means \"not a browser\" so the check cannot meaningfully apply. Caught by SpawnDev.WebTorrent PlaywrightMultiTest after the 2026-04-24 hub.spawndev.com allowlist deployment 403'd 5 desktop tests; new `OriginAllowlist_E2E_MissingOriginBypassesList` E2E test in the SpawnDev.RTC suite locks the new behavior. Browser clients still allowlist-checked as before. See SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.6 for the full write-up.",
